From bdd106b3c38a01b74c875198fc0622932a9e8261 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 08:54:03 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(kanban): omit sweep time from registry evidence identity
 [daveey]

The minute-boundary fix alone was insufficient: raw CI occurrence-35 comment
seconds were 1794798490/1794798491 (10/11 seconds within a minute). The registry
body independently interpolates _now_ms() to the second, so an unchanged
registry also bypasses exact-body comment dedup on every second boundary.

Remove that rendering-time stamp for readable and unreadable registries.
Task/comment created_at preserves observation time; all actual registry fields
remain in the evidence. Extend the regression to advance the narrow module
clock (not global time) across second-only and minute boundaries. Retain skip
updates, target expansion, distinct causes, and verify registry field changes
still alter evidence.

RED after minute-only fix: all 16 boundary/cause/target rows fail (3 vs 2).
Final GREEN: all 16 importing test files, 315 passed via hermes-core-wt test.
Full scripts/check --base origin/main passed. Raw CI logs and both independent
RED logs are in task t_21bdb628627b563e's evidence. No sleeps or retries added.
